cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Multi-asset factor risk model with a cost-aware implementation layer"
abstract: >-
  Two factor risk models -- a macro multi-asset model and a cross-sectional
  equity model -- sharing one asset-class-agnostic covariance pipeline (EWMA with
  separated half-lives, Newey-West, eigenfactor risk adjustment, volatility
  regime adjustment, specific risk), wrapped in a cost-aware convex optimizer
  with a time-varying, empirically calibrated transaction-cost model. It
  decomposes the gap between a model portfolio's paper and realised Sharpe ratio
  into a risk-model term and a cost term, and contrasts the two panels to
  separate specification error from estimation error in the bias statistic.
  Reproducible from free data through a committed manifest.
authors:
